cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use or reference URML (the Universal Robot Language) in academic
  work, please cite it using these metadata.
title: "URML — Universal Robot Language"
abstract: >-
  An open specification and reference implementation for describing robot
  intent: a small, human-readable language that sits above robot operating
  systems (ROS 2, PX4, vendor SDKs) and below language models. Every URML
  program is statically verified against the robot's declared capabilities,
  the active safety envelope, and a deployment compliance policy before any
  actuator moves.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ido
    family-names: Yahalomi
    email: greenvh@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/URML-MARS/URML"
url: "https://github.com/URML-MARS/URML"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - robotics
  - large language models
  - formal verification
  - ROS 2
  - PX4
  - robot safety
